    "raw_text": "\n<think>\nmulti-dimensional analysis:\nLet me analyze this video based on the provided frames and the text prompt. The prompt asks for \"a 15-second, 16:9 horizontal video depicting a paper craft stop-motion animation workshop with a male carpenter in gray/blue work clothes, holding a wooden mallet, standing at a workbench with a thick wooden board, side lighting, static background, and no additional elements.\" \n\nVisual Quality Analysis:\nThe video adopts a stylized 3D animation aesthetic rather than a strict photorealistic look. Visual quality is moderate overall (score 3): details are generally clear, but there are occasional minor artifacts and slight softness that prevent a higher rating. Lighting remains consistent across most frames, with stable shading and color balance; a few frames show minor texture inconsistencies or subtle motion blur during rapid hand movements. The character design is clean and readable, and the workshop environment reads clearly, though some surfaces could benefit from crisper micro-details. Overall, the visuals are coherent and serviceable, but not outstanding.\n\nText-to-Video Alignment Analysis:\nAlignment to the prompt is strong overall (score 4). The scene captures the core elements: a male carpenter in gray/blue work clothes, holding a wooden mallet, at a workbench with a thick wooden board, under side lighting, with a static background and no extraneous elements. The framing is close to 16:9 and the sequence follows a logical workflow of actions. There may be minor deviations in exact timing or pose, but these do not significantly detract from the alignment.\n\nPhysical/Common-sense Consistency:\nPhysical consistency is moderate (score 3). The hammering action and tool handling feel plausible within the stylized animation, and the character’s proportions remain coherent throughout. However, some motions appear slightly stiff or exaggerated due to the stylization, and a few interactions (e.g., weight transfer during the swing, or the board’s response to impact) are not perfectly physically accurate. Overall, the scene maintains believable dynamics without breaking immersion.\n</think>\n\n(1) visual quality: 3\n(2) text-to-video alignment: 4\n(3) physical/common-sense consistency: 3\n"
